course: dictionary
lesson: 3126
title: Electronic: machines that run on circuits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Electronic describes machines and devices that work using tiny electric circuits and chips, like phones, computers and games. «The first electronic computers of the 1940s filled whole rooms» tells you these machines were built from electric parts, not from springs or gears.
explain: Electronic can also describe things done or stored on a computer. Electronic mail is a message sent through a computer, and electronic money is money kept and moved on computers. The words near it, such as «computers» or «devices», are the clues that show which meaning fits.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «electronic» in place of «old» in «an old game» and see if it fits. Electronic games need a battery or charging, so the word points to things that run on power and chips.
fact: Electronic means working with tiny electric circuits and chips.
fact: «Colossus» was built at Bletchley Park in 1943 to 1944 and was one of the first electronic computers.
fact: Colossus helped break the German code Lorenz, not Enigma.
fact: In the 1940s, six women programmed ENIAC, one of the first electronic computers.
fact: Electronic devices like phones and games often need batteries or charging.
exercise: «The first electronic computers of the 1940s filled whole rooms.» What does electronic describe here? | *Machines that work using electric circuits and chips | Wooden toys made by hand | Paper letters sent by post | Plants that grow in gardens
exercise: Mum says, «Check the electronic register for your lesson.» What is an electronic register? | Pots and pans in the kitchen | *A list kept and checked on a computer | A type of bicycle bell | A book of old maps
exercise: Which phrase uses electronic to mean something stored or sent on a computer? | Wooden train set | *Electronic mail | Paper map of the hills | Stone garden wall
test: «Colossus helped break a different German code, Lorenz, not Enigma.» What does this tell you about Colossus? | *It was a machine used to break a German code | It was a type of paper map | It was a German ship | It was a children's song
test: Ella says electronic games need batteries. Which clue best shows she is right? | Games are fun to play outside | Games have bright colours | Games are played with friends | *Electronic games use electric circuits, so they need power
exam: Which word in «six women programmed ENIAC, one of the first electronic computers» shows that ENIAC was a machine? | *computers | programmed | women | first
